blocks:
  - type: metin
    baslik: The difference between sadness and depression
    metin: |-
      Sadness is usually a temporary emotion triggered by a specific event — a loss, disappointment or failure. It eases with time and support, and the person retains some enjoyment of life.

      Depression is different: the low mood does not lift, it persists without a clear cause or out of proportion to circumstances, and the person can no longer enjoy things they once found pleasurable. This disrupts everyday functioning.

      The American Psychological Association (APA) defines depression as a negative emotional state, ranging from unhappiness and discontent to an extreme feeling of sadness, pessimism and despondency, that interferes with daily life. Changes in eating or sleeping habits, lack of energy or motivation, difficulty concentrating or making decisions, and withdrawal from social activities often come with it ([APA](https://www.apa.org/topics/depression)).
  - type: bilgi-kutusu
    ton: yesil
    baslik: The two-week marker
    metin: The World Health Organization (WHO) distinguishes a depressive episode from ordinary mood fluctuations. During an episode, low mood or a loss of interest and pleasure lasts most of the day, nearly every day, for at least two weeks. Depression can happen to anyone; the WHO also notes that women are affected more often than men ([WHO](https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/depression)).
  - type: kart-grid
    baslik: Symptoms of depression
    kolon: 3
    kartlar:
      - baslik: Emotional
        maddeler:
          - Persistent sadness or emptiness
          - Loss of interest or pleasure
          - Feelings of worthlessness
          - Excessive guilt
          - Hopelessness, helplessness
          - Thoughts of death or suicide
      - baslik: Cognitive
        maddeler:
          - Difficulty concentrating
          - Trouble making decisions
          - Negative thought patterns
          - Memory problems
          - Self-criticism
      - baslik: Physical
        maddeler:
          - Sleep changes (too much or too little)
          - Appetite changes
          - Fatigue, loss of energy
          - Psychomotor slowing
          - Unexplained aches and pains
  - type: kart-yigini
    baslik: Types of depression
    kartlar:
      - baslik: Major Depressive Disorder
        metin: The most widely recognised type. Symptoms last at least two weeks and significantly impair daily functioning. Episodes may recur.
      - baslik: Dysthymia (Persistent Depressive Disorder)
        metin: A milder but chronic form of depression that can last for years. The feeling of "I've always been this way" is common.
      - baslik: Seasonal Affective Disorder
        metin: Begins in autumn–winter and resolves in spring.
      - baslik: Postpartum Depression
        metin: Develops after childbirth and is far more severe and prolonged than the "baby blues".
  - type: kart-grid
    baslik: Causes
    giris: 'Depression cannot be attributed to a single cause. It is understood within a biopsychosocial model:'
    kolon: 3
    kartlar:
      - baslik: Biological
        maddeler:
          - Genetic predisposition
          - Serotonin and dopamine imbalances
          - Thyroid and hormonal issues
          - Chronic illness
      - baslik: Psychological
        maddeler:
          - Negative thought schemas
          - Low self-efficacy
          - Past trauma or losses
          - Perfectionism
      - baslik: Social
        maddeler:
          - Loneliness, isolation
          - Relationship difficulties
          - Work or financial stress
          - Weak support network
  - type: onayli-liste
    baslik: Treatment options
    giris: 'The main approaches used when working with depression:'
    maddeler:
      - baslik: Cognitive Behavioural Therapy (CBT)
        aciklama: Focuses on identifying and changing the negative thought patterns that fuel depression.
      - baslik: Antidepressant Medication
        aciklama: Prescribed following [psychiatric evaluation](/en/blog/psychologist-or-psychiatrist.html). Whether medication runs alongside therapy is discussed in that evaluation.
      - baslik: Trauma-Focused Therapy
        aciklama: Addresses underlying traumatic experiences to support long-term recovery from depression. This work usually runs within [individual therapy](/en/services/individual-therapy.html).
      - baslik: Lifestyle Changes
        aciklama: Regular exercise, sleep hygiene and social connection are important factors that support the treatment process. For the talking-therapy side, see [CBT therapy](/en/services/cbt-therapy.html).
  - type: bilgi-kutusu
    ton: turuncu
    baslik: If you are having thoughts of harming yourself or others
    metin: Please contact a healthcare provider or someone you trust immediately. These thoughts are a symptom of depression and can improve with help.
